+## Retained replay and projection checkpoint — draft, 2026-10-04
+
+The combined candidate requires persisted replay-request evidence, records
+canonical CT32 plus the terminal occurrence through QMB's exclusive writer,
+and verifies existing artifacts before completed invocation recovery. Direct
+projection reopens original pinned CT29/CT32/context without replay or backfill;
+nonzero child query exit is refused. An operator local environment declaration
+neither registers an actor nor establishes CT47 authoring authority.
+
+Public `qmb.analysis.project` still needs a host-owned selector/context bridge.
+Current public ExperimentSpec identity and QMB resolved-run identity differ.
+The proposed compatible extension names a resolved-run selector explicitly,
+refuses ambiguous/crossowner results, and preserves read query occupancy.
+Coordinated ledger publication remains dispatched-Agent work. No dummy model
+deployment or fixture identity substitutes for legitimate authoring.
